Context ​
Counting is an essential skill that all children need to learn. ​
Children enjoy using interactive devices that require them to count. ​
Your task is to identify a solution to the problem outlined below and to produce an engineered prototype device or system to help solve the problem. ​

In addition to the problem, there are three examples of how the problem could be solved. You can choose a solution from this list, or you can create your own. ​
Your solution must include both mechanical and electronic components to provide an integrated product. ​



Problem ​
Counting can be a challenging skill for children to learn. Your task is to engineer a device or system that will support children with learning how to count. ​

Three examples of possible solutions: ​
  - Engineer a prototype device or system that will support children with counting money.​
  - Engineer a prototype device or system that will support children with sorting and counting objects. ​
  - Engineer a prototype device or system that will help children to count and weigh items.
